From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] q706f: dts: disable the QCE node (no driver; blocks interconnect sync_state)

CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_QCE is not set, so crypto@1dfa000 never binds:
  qnoc-sm8250 163d000.interconnect: sync_state() pending due to 1dfa000.crypto
  qnoc-sm8250 1700000.interconnect: sync_state() pending due to 1dfa000.crypto
icc_sync_state() only drops the boot votes once every provider is synced,
so all interconnect nodes keep avg/peak = INT_MAX in every RPMh bucket
(interconnect_summary shows 2147483647 on each node). The buses and the DDR
stay at their top corner in s2idle as well: qcom_stats cxsd/aosd/ddr = 0.

The alternative is to build the driver (CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_QCE=m); it is not
needed here (ARMv8 CE is faster) and it registers extra crypto algorithms.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
index cc6abe92b7de004fbfa030cfbfd10224a3556735..4855787d0a102922be7f3bc41e8fc5e7623a8247 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
@@ -823,8 +823,14 @@ opp-3187200000 {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * No QCE driver is built (CONFIG_CRYPTO_DEV_QCE is not set). An enabled node
+ * without a driver keeps the aggre2_noc and mc_virt interconnect providers
+ * from ever reaching sync_state(), which leaves every interconnect node at
+ * its INT_MAX boot vote, in the RPMh sleep set too (no CX collapse in s2idle).
+ */
 &crypto {
-	status = "okay";
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &gmu {
